            <ArticleTitle>Shortcomings of coronary angiography and their implications in clinical practice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>479-85</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Physicians must interpret coronary angiography with caution and skepticism. Coronary angiography is considered the gold standard for defining coronary artery anatomy, diagnosing coronary artery disease, and guiding intervention. However, it does not provide functional information and may be misleading.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
